  "geometry_notes": [
   "Widths 36/48 in; depths 12/17/21/27/33/42 in (sections 1-6); section 1 (12 in) is solid.",
   "5 in webs and 5 1/2 in top/bottom slabs printed; void chamfers 1 1/2 x 1 1/2 in (sections 2-3) and 3 x 3 in (sections 4-6); 3/4 in soffit chamfers.",
   "ESTIMATE: the shear-key recess detail prints 4 in (top band), 3/8 in, 3/4 in and 3 in (bottom band) without an unambiguous recess depth. Modelled as a 3/4 in recess from 4 in below the top to 3 in above the soffit with 45-degree transitions, and the printed 5 in web measured from the recessed face (the 42 in drawing places the 5 in arrow on the recessed face). This interpretation makes the area residual depth-independent (+3.1 to +3.6 in2), which the alternative (web from the full face) does not.",
   "Residual pattern: modelled area +0.5 to +0.8% and Ix +0.6 to +1.0% above Table 19.3-3 for every row; the published yb (from St/Sb) sits 0.01-0.04 in BELOW mid-depth whereas the drawn key (4 in band on top, 3 in band at bottom) puts it 0.01-0.04 in above. The table appears to use a slightly different (possibly inverted) key idealisation; pinned as one systematic discrepancy, not hidden.",
   "The keyway is omitted on the exterior face of exterior girders; the profile here is the interior (both faces keyed) unit."
  ],
